  "fullPassage": "During New York Fashion Week 2018, a woman with a brightly decorated prosthetic leg proudly walked the runway at a major fashion show. She was Mama Cax, a model and influencer.\n\nCax was diagnosed with cancer at age 14 and lost her right leg at 16 after surgery. At first, Cax was depressed and struggled to accept her new body. However, with the support of her family and friends, Cax learned to love it. One day when she was 26, Cax posted a picture on social media showing her leg. \"I didn't think it could help anyone,\" she said in an interview, \"But after receiving messages of support, I realized my story could inspire others.\" After receiving support from others, she began to use social media to share more about her life and to inspire others. She proudly posted pictures of herself wearing stylish prosthetic covers and spoke out about body positivity and fashion. In 2016, she became the first model for the #RunwayForAll campaign. In 2018, she appeared on the cover of major fashion magazines.\n\nWhen asked, \"How did you come to embrace yourself?\" she replied, \"The truth is, like many people, I'm still on my journey to self-love. There are many barriers ahead.\" In addition to modeling, Cax showed her ability to overcome physical barriers by swimming, playing basketball, and mountain climbing. She even finished the New York City Marathon in a wheelchair.\n\nSadly, Mama Cax's journey was cut short in 2019. Although she is no longer with us, her journey will remain in our hearts, inspiring us to overcome limitations and find our own paths to success and happiness.",
  "title": "A Journey to Self-Love",
